191:- <a id="decided-2026-11-05-q6-2-fields"></a>**Q6.2 and R4 F12, known values through structs** (owner-approved revision, 2026-11-05, made during A2b): known values propagate field by field through immutable struct construction and destructuring. The checker tracks an abstract value for each binding: unknown, a known scalar, or a constructor whose fields carry their own abstract values. Constructing a struct records each field's fact independently; an immutable binding keeps the fact; destructuring hands each field's fact, recursively, to the corresponding immutable binder; an unknown component stays unknown without discarding its known siblings; an ownership transfer keeps the facts for the receiving binding without permitting reuse of the consumed one. Q6.2's exclusions stay (mutable state, branches and paths, user-function calls, calls outside the table, elaborator temporaries). So `let S { a } = S { a: 200u8 }; a + 100` is refused, in trusted and unreachable code too (OD118 as revised by Q6.4). Before this revision a field bound by destructuring was not known and that program was accepted and trapped.
294:- **P6** Retention manifest gates deleting legacy/ — RETENTION.tsv at the root gives every legacy asset (corpus, regressions, examples, std, bug ledger, site, docs, research) a destination and deletion criterion. Revised 2026-11-06 ([restart row](#decided-project-restart)): nothing is deleted at B3; legacy/, the old pipeline included, is deleted way later (LD: once the new compiler implements a full real program such as RocksDB, ethrex or similar), when RETENTION.tsv has no live entry, a final ideas sweep has dispositioned every idea and the owner explicitly approves.
312:- **P23** Precedence between decisions, rows and drafts — Recorded decisions govern. An accepted row supersedes a recorded rule only through an explicitly identified, owner-approved revision (Q5.1/Q5.4 for OD45/OD87, Q6.4 for TYPE-22, Q2.8 for TRAIT-1, Q9.15/P3 for generated chapters). R4's replacements govern conflicting draft recommendations. Before your acceptance is recorded, every passage R4 F18 lists is reconciled (capability inference, generated chapters, roadmap authority, assurance wording, restart order and retention, Phase E, freeze dependencies, superseded Core recommendations), and historical conflicting text is marked superseded.
